/-! # S5 Universal-Cluster Tableau Simplification

This module defines the S5 "propagate box to ALL branch worlds" universal rule
(`modalApplyOneS5`), which realises S5's single-cluster model property directly, without any
loop-checking machinery (unlike S4, `LoopChecking.lean`). It instantiates the generic tableau
driver (`Saturation.lean`'s `modalStepBranchGen`/`modalExpandBranchesGen`/`modalTableauGen`) at
`modalApplyOneS5`, mirroring the B-system build (`FrameRules.lean`/`BDriver.lean`)
declaration-for-declaration.

## Main Definitions

- `modalS5BoxAll`/`modalS5DiaNegAll`: the two universal-propagation helpers. From `T(□φ)@w`,
  emit `T(φ)@w'` for **every** known world `w'` of the branch (not just `w` itself, unlike T's
  self-propagation; not just recorded predecessors, unlike B's backward propagation), filtered
  to exclude formulas already present. Dually for `F(◇φ)@w`.
- `modalApplyOneS5`: apply the K rules (`modalApplyOne`) together with the S5 universal
  propagation arms, merging persistent-rule outputs. Reduces to `modalApplyOne` exactly outside
  the two S5-relevant signed-formula shapes (`T(□φ)@w`, `F(◇φ)@w`).
- `modalApplyOneS5w`: the **witness-reuse** rule. At the
  two mint shapes it reuses an existing witness world when the `(sign, formula)` tag is already
  present, instead of K's unconditional fresh mint, capping world creation at `modalOps φ` and so
  at K's own `modalWorldBound φ`. This is the rule the shipped decision procedure runs.
- `modalStepBranchS5`/`modalExpandBranchesS5`/`modalTableauS5`: the S5-system driver. The two step
  helpers are instantiated at `apply := modalApplyOneS5`; the shipped **decision procedure**
  `modalTableauS5` is instantiated at `apply := modalApplyOneS5w`, which terminates at K's fuel.
  Its soundness (`modalTableauS5_sound`, `FrameSoundness.lean`) and completeness/decidability
  (`modalTableauS5_complete`/`s5Valid_decides`/`instDecidableS5Valid`, `FrameCompleteness.lean`)
  are the S5 capstone.

## Strategy

`modalApplyOneS5` agrees with `modalApplyOne` (K) outside the two S5-relevant signed-formula
shapes (`modalApplyOneS5_eq_of_not_boxPos_diaNeg`), so every `RuleApplicationSpec` field's "not
shaped" case reduces directly to the corresponding K witness. **At the two S5-relevant shapes
specifically** (`T(□φ)@w`, `F(◇φ)@w` -- universal propagation), `modalApplyOneS5` never mints a
world (its accessibility output is exactly K's, unchanged) and only ever appends
universally-propagated formulas at **existing known worlds** of the branch -- this is
structurally *simpler* than B's predecessor-restricted backward propagation, since the
target-world bound follows directly from `modalKnownWorlds b`'s own bound (`label_le_modalMaxWorld`)
with no `accFreshInv`/edge-tracing detour, and the known-worlds membership (F6) is immediate by
construction (the propagation is generated by iterating over `modalKnownWorlds b` itself).

**This does NOT mean `modalApplyOneS5` overall never mints a world.** At the two K-inherited MINT
shapes (`T(◇φ)@w`, `F(□φ)@w`), `modalApplyOneS5` falls through unchanged to K's own
unconditional, witness-free mint -- and because the S5 propagation above keeps manufacturing
fresh triggers for those mint shapes every cycle, this minting is **unbounded**
(`modalApplyOneS5_hintikka_not_reachable_growth`, the R7 refutation below): `modalFuel` does
**not** dominate the unguarded expansion. This is exactly why the witness-reuse rule
`modalApplyOneS5w` exists: it replaces minting with reuse at precisely these two shapes, leaving
the propagation shapes above untouched.

## References

* [M. Fitting, *Proof Methods for Modal and Intuitionistic Logics*][Fitting1983], Chapter 2
* [R. Goré, *Tableau Methods for Modal and Temporal Logics*][Gore1999], technical-report
  pagination: the divergence of the unguarded universal rule under a naive depth measure (TR
  p.48), and the linear single-cluster model graph `|W| = 1 + m` the witness rule realises
  (TR pp.44-45) -- `m` the count of distinct diamond/box mint triggers, here `modalOps φ₀`.
* [P. Blackburn, M. de Rijke, Y. Venema, *Modal Logic*][Blackburn2001], §6.6 p.382: the `m + 1`
  selection-of-points world bound for S5 and S5's NP-completeness (the decidability delivered by
  `instDecidableS5Valid`, `FrameCompleteness.lean`).
-/

@[expose] public section

